*.csv
*.tsv
*.h5

# The asset coverage inventory is the deliberate exception to the "no tables"
# rule above: five small TSVs (~510 kB total) that say what has been acquired
# vs. what the pipeline consumed. They are infrastructure, not results — worth
# having in history so asset drift (a dataset appearing, content going missing
# upstream) is visible as a diff rather than only on the machine that ran it.
!inventory/*.tsv

# Figures are the deliberate exception to "no binaries" below: small
# (~1.2 MB total), genuinely useful to diff/review across pipeline runs, and
# the actual scientific output of this project. Tracked, not ignored.
!*.png

# Guard: no step writes a volume here, but keep this so a stray image can never
# be committed by accident. Derived outputs inherit their inputs' sensitivity.
*.nii
*.nii.gz

# panel_sizes.json is fully derived from connectome_figure.svg (which is
# tracked) and regenerated on every run — no need to also track it.
figures/panel_sizes.json

# The inventory dashboard is fully derived from the (ignored) inventory TSVs
# and re-rendered on every run — tracking it would be pure churn. Same reasoning
# as figures/panel_sizes.json above.
inventory/inventory_dashboard.html

# Provenance is a tracked output: it records what produced everything else.
!PROVENANCE.json
